Internet Not Working


Can you open any website?
Are others experiencing this? 
Does Wi-Fi/Ethernet show "Connected”? Are you on Wi-Fi / Ethernet
Is the network icon showing an error?
internet vs local network? Can you access local resources (shared drive, printer, router page)
	
                     Issue

Users could not access the internet despite the system showing an active network connection (Wi-Fi/Ethernet icon shows: No Internet or Limited Connectivity)
Webpages won’t load in any browser
Other apps cannot connect to the internet

                    Cause
DNS misconfiguration on the network adapter prevented domain name resolution.
Cached bad DNS entries
Network adapter disabled, misconfigured, or driver issue
IP conflict or incorrect network settings


                   Steps / Resolution
Verified network connection status
Check physical network connection (Wi-Fi or Ethernet cable)
Other devices are connected/have internet or no issues




Run ipconfig /all to check IP address, subnet, gateway, and DNS
This will show all your network adapters and their settings. Focus on the adapter that is connected (Wi-Fi or Ethernet)

Reviewed IP configuration with ipconfig /all  = IP address, subnet, gateway, and DNS
IP address = 192.168.65	 Range:(192.168.1.1 - 192.168.1.254) 
